  "trigger_name": "CFSR Monitoring",
  "summary_html": "Federal **Child and Family Services Reviews (CFSR)** monitor state performance on safety, permanency, and well-being. Project Milk Carton flags states that repeatedly fail or never publish CFSR improvement plans. Michigan is also under federal court oversight in Dwayne B. v. Whitmer (E.D. Mich. No. 2:06-cv-13548), settled as a consent decree approved 24 October 2008 and now governed by the Modified Implementation, Sustainability and Exit Plan (MISEP), under court-appointed monitors Kevin Ryan and Eileen Crummy of Public Catalyst. In the MISEP 28 report (issued 31 July 2026, covering January–June 2025) the monitors assessed that the quality of state oversight \"left unresolved risks to youth safety at certain contracted CCIs and CPAs,\" and reported that 42 of 46 child placing agency inspections in the period required corrective action plans.",
  "authority_html": "- **45 CFR Part 1355** — CFSR procedures and performance metrics  \n- **Social Security Act IV-E (42 U.S.C. §§ 670–679c)** — ties funding to CFSR compliance",
